tPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2432,"endPos":2480,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":68,"length":49}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2487,"endPos":2590,"startLine":67,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":67,"endLineOffset":123,"length":104}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":67,"line":67,"comment_lines":["[][67]"],"review_comment":["If we no longer consider `IndexNotFoundException` irrecoverable, could we modify the `isExceptionIrrecoverable` method to reflect that instead of adding the `isNotIndexNotFoundException` method?\r\n\r\nOr the distinction is still needed for cases other than bulk responses?","That is a good question - at least for now I was thinking of just handling it for the destination index? The source index can still fail with IndexNotFoundException (if PIT \u003d\u003d null): https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/main/x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/transforms/ClientTransformIndexer.java#L602\r\n\r\nI haven\u0027t seen this same type of intermittent failure scenario though, where the source index gets relocated to a new shard and the request fails on the old shard, so I\u0027m not sure if we just haven\u0027t seen it yet or if search behaves differently where the request will automatically reroute.","\u003e I\u0027m not sure if we just haven\u0027t seen it yet or if search behaves differently where the request will automatically reroute.\r\n\r\nI don\u0027t know either unfortunately :(\r\nBut since we are going in a direction to make more errors recoverable (and more transforms unattended) it could make sense to make `IndexNotFoundException` recoverable.\r\nBut maybe let\u0027s not do it in this PR if you don\u0027t feel comfortable.\r\nWe can leave this PR for dealing with destination index only.\r\nPlease make it clear in the PR title/description."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","id":37106,"created_at":"2024-05-09T11:29:00Z","original_position":13,"side":"RIGHT","position":13,"submitted_on_commit":"1211b0a783364942412f5a3aeaea4167a51dd6e2","diff_hunk":"@@ -63,7 +64,7 @@ public static Throwable getFirstIrrecoverableExceptionFromBulkResponses(Collecti\n             }\n \n             if (unwrappedThrowable instanceof ElasticsearchException elasticsearchException) {\n-                if (isExceptionIrrecoverable(elasticsearchException)) {\n+                if (isExceptionIrrecoverable(elasticsearchException) \u0026\u0026 isNotIndexNotFoundException(elasticsearchException)) {","submitted_line":67},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change in `getFirstIrrecoverableExceptionFromBulkResponses` introduces a new method `isNotIndexNotFoundException`. While this makes the code more readable, it also adds an additional layer of abstraction. It is important to balance readability with the complexity introduced by additional methods. In this case, the addition seems justified due to the clarity it provides.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java-x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java-2432:2480-2487:2590","promptId":"#NCBCY","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/utils/ExceptionRootCauseFinder.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":2432,"endPos":2480,"startLine":66,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":66,"endLineOffset":68,"length":49}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2487,"endPos":2590,"startLine":67,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":67,"endLineOffset":123,"length":104}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":9